{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall return unto HaShem your Elohim.</b> It says ״וְשַׁבְתָּ,״ and it was not sufficient with what it said, ״וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶךָ,״ according to what I explained — that ״וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶךָ״ and so forth is the rebuttal to his erring heart, meaning to recognize that he has not done well; whereas the return before HaShem to improve his ways is the statement of ״וְשַׁבְתָּ עַד.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:15.587830384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}